      "title": "Globe Life Q3 Earnings Miss Estimates on Weak Underwriting Income",
      "summary": "Globe Life reported Q3 2026 operating EPS of $4.84, slightly missing estimates but growing 0.6% year-over-year. Premium revenues rose 6.5%, but underwriting income fell 4.2% and expenses surged 11.5%, pressuring profitability. The company revised its 2026 EPS guidance downward to $15.35-$15.65 due to adverse results at United American, while raising share repurchase forecasts. Book value per share increased 22.8% year-over-year.",
